message: "If you use this work or its derived data, please cite it as below."
title: "US Care Safety Signals"
abstract: >-
  Analyses of public US federal data on injuries to caregivers and harm to
  patients during patient handling and transfer in hospitals and nursing
  facilities. Modules cover resident-handling injuries (5,654 of 25,860
  nursing-facility cases reported to OSHA for 2025), the handling task under
  way in hospitals and nursing facilities (about 1,440 hospital injuries
  during lateral transfers between surfaces), lifting equipment mentioned in
  injury narratives, violence against caregivers, patient harm in 14,439 FDA
  MAUDE reports for patient lifts, transfer devices, and stretchers
  (2015-2025), hospital-acquired pressure injury and HACRP penalties across
  3,056 hospitals, a graded crosswalk linking 8,047 OSHA establishments to
  CMS-certified nursing homes, and an out-of-sample validation against OSHA's
  OIICS coding. Every text-classification rule is validated against blind
  human review. Facilities are identified by federal identifier and state
  only; no product or manufacturer is named.
type: dataset
